---
import Footer from '@/components/Footer.astro'
import Header from '@/components/Header.astro'
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro'

const pageTitle = 'Contact'
const pageDescription = 'Use the contact details below for general enquiries, editorial notes, and site-related questions.'
---

<Layout>
  <Header />
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <header class="mb-12 space-y-4">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-primary">Pages</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">{pageTitle}</h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-muted-foreground">{pageDescription}</p>
    </header>

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Available contact routes</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-7">Use [CONTACT_EMAIL] for general enquiries, editorial notes, and messages that do not need a public reply.</p>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-7">If a newsletter is added later, it should be kept separate from general contact requests.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">What you can send here</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-7">Use the published email route for general enquiries, corrections, or messages that do not need a formal support queue.</p>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-7">The contact page is best suited to questions about general enquiries, business questions, and communication connected to the website.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Response expectations</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-7">Responses, when they are provided, will depend on the type of enquiry and the availability of the editorial team.</p>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-7">No guaranteed response window is implied unless the site later publishes one as part of a real support or business workflow.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Privacy note</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-7">Contact messages should be treated as operational communication rather than as public content.</p>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-7">If more formal handling is required later, the site can add a specific retention or routing policy without changing the basic page structure.</p>
      </section>
      <aside class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-muted p-4 text-sm text-muted-foreground">
        <p>This starter page is generated as a baseline and should be reviewed and customized before being relied on as production legal or business copy.</p>
      </aside>
  </article>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
